      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Surgical excision is the standard treatment for chronic pilonidal disease, but all excisional techniques are associated with tissue loss, risk of wound break down, and chronic healing problems."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "The aim of the study was to compare sinus excision and primary closure vs a laying open technique in a prospective randomized trial."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN, PATIENTS, AND INTERVENTIONS",
          "content": "Eighty patients were randomly assigned to sinus excision and primary closure (n = 39) or laying open (n = 41). Follow-up was performed 1, 3, and 12 months after surgery."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MAIN OUTCOME MEASURE",
          "content": "The main outcome measure was the healing rate after 1 year."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The healing rate was significantly higher after excision and closure than after laying open at 1 month (20 of 39 vs 8 of 41; P = .005) and 3 months (36 of 38 vs 28 of 39; P = .013) after surgery. At follow-up 12 months after surgery no difference was seen in healing rate between the treatment arms (33 of 37 vs 37 of 38; P = .198)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "This prospective randomized trial shows that sinus excision and primary closure results in faster healing than laying open does, but there is no difference in healing rate after 1 year. The laying open procedure is minimally invasive with small risks for the patient, and it might therefore be considered more frequently as the first choice of treatment (www.clinicaltrials.gov. Unique identifier: NCT00997048)."
        }
      ]},
